%% alt: The application sends messages and tool definitions; the model returns a tool call with a name and JSON arguments; the application checks the schema and the user's permissions, runs the tool, and sends back the result, which is untrusted input; the loop repeats until the model gives a final answer.
flowchart TB
  U[User request]:::human --> A[Your code<br/>sends messages and<br/>tool definitions]:::tool
  A --> M[Model]:::model
  M -->|tool call| V{Schema valid?<br/>User allowed?}:::control
  M -->|finished| F[Final answer]:::human
  V -->|yes| T[Run the tool]:::tool
  V -->|no| E[Return an error<br/>as the result]:::tool
  T --> R[Tool result<br/>untrusted input]:::untrusted
  R -.-> A
  E -.-> A
